#!/bin/sh
#
# Refuses a commit that stages a credential.
#
# CI scans the full history on every push and will catch this too — but only
# after the secret has reached the remote, at which point the commit is
# cloneable and the credential has to be rotated whatever happens next. This
# repository is private on the Free plan, so GitHub's own push protection is
# not available; closing the window locally is what is available.
#
# Same binary, same `.gitleaks.toml` as CI. A hook that disagreed with the
# server would be worse than none, because a local pass would stop meaning
# anything.
set -eu

CONFIG="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.gitleaks.toml"
LOCAL_BIN="$(git rev-parse --git-dir)/hooks-bin/gitleaks"

if [ -x "$LOCAL_BIN" ]; then
  GITLEAKS="$LOCAL_BIN"
elif command -v gitleaks >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  GITLEAKS=gitleaks
else
  cat >&2 <<'MESSAGE'

  gitleaks is not installed, so staged changes cannot be scanned.

  Install it with either:

      pnpm hooks:install     # pinned to the version CI uses, checksum-verified
      brew install gitleaks

  This hook fails rather than passing quietly. A secret check that skips
  itself when the tool is missing reports success on every commit, which is
  the one outcome worse than not having it.

MESSAGE
  exit 1
fi

# `--staged` scans what is about to be committed, not the working tree, so an
# unstaged scratch file with a token in it does not block unrelated work.
if ! "$GITLEAKS" protect --staged --redact --config "$CONFIG"; then
  cat >&2 <<'MESSAGE'

  A staged change looks like a credential, so the commit was stopped.

  If it is real: do not commit it, and rotate it if it has ever been pushed.
  Deleting the commit later does not invalidate a credential, and rewriting
  history does not reach clones that already have it.

  If it is a false positive: add a narrow rule to .gitleaks.toml explaining
  why the value is not a secret. Do not widen the allowlist to make the
  message go away, and do not reach for --no-verify: CI runs the same scan
  over the full history and will fail there instead.

MESSAGE
  exit 1
fi
